// SOUNDNESS QUEUE row zonemut_fat_ref_struct_field_layout_abort (tier 3).
// A `&mut T` to a `#[zone_mut]` T is a FAT {data, zone} pair (16 B). Put that
// type in a STRUCT FIELD and logosc ABORTS — rc 134, core dumped, before any
// codegen — because layout_of counts the field fat and llvm::DataLayout builds
// it thin:
//   LLVM ERROR: the compiler's layout engines disagree ...
//     [emitted] q.H: size — layout_of says 16, llvm::DataLayout says 8
// NO construction, no use, no LOGOS_VERIFY_LAYOUT is needed: the struct
// DECLARATION alone aborts, which is why this shape cannot be a fail fixture
// either (a fail fixture asserts a diagnostic, and the compiler dies instead).
//
// ⚠ THE CLASS, ENUMERATED BY THE PROPERTY 2026-09-08 on build 2c5a33ef99e94fc9
// 43: 12 declaration shapes plus 3 runtime programs. The property is "a Fat
// ZoneMut `&mut` reaching the LLVM STRUCT TYPE BUILDER as a member". Every
// failing shape prints the same two-engine disagreement, so it is ONE site.
//   FAIL (5), all rc 134:
//     * a named struct field, `struct H { r: &mut Box2 }` — this program;
//     * a TUPLE-STRUCT field, `struct H(&mut Box2);`;
//     * a NESTED field, `struct Inner { r: &mut Box2 } struct Outer { i: Inner }`
//       — the abort names `Inner`, the innermost carrier;
//     * a GENERIC struct instantiated at it, `struct W<T> { r: T }` used at
//       `W<&mut Box2>` — the abort names the mono'd `W$G1$refmut_Box2`;
//     * the same field inside a `#[zone_mut]` struct.
//   OK (7):
//     * an ENUM PAYLOAD, `enum E { N, S(&mut Box2) }`, and the generic enum
//       `Opt<&mut Box2>` — the enum lowering path does not disagree. ⚠ AND IT
//       IS NOT SILENTLY THIN: built, matched, `zone_of` read back through the
//       payload binder, RUN rc 0, `LOGOS_VERIFY_LAYOUT=1` 0 disagreements
//       (the enum is given a NICHE layout over the 16-byte payload). So the
//       enum path is correct, not merely quiet — this is the shape that would
//       have been a tier-1 row had it dropped the zone half, and it does not.
//     * a TUPLE local `(&mut Box2, i64)` and an ARRAY local `[&mut Box2; 1]`,
//       both also RUN with `zone_of` read back: rc 0.
//     * a bare fn parameter `fn take(r: &mut Box2)`;
//     * a SHARED `&Box2` field (a shared ref to a #[zone_mut] type stays thin);
//     * the same struct with `#[zone_mut]` removed (thin `&mut` field).
//
// ⚠ EXTENDS THE ROW AS MINTED EARLIER THE SAME DAY (commit db2fa5f96), which
// said "It is the FIELD position alone" off four clean shapes. The verdict
// stands and is now positive rather than residual: four MORE aggregate-field
// spellings abort (tuple-struct, nested, generic instantiation, zone_mut
// struct), and the nearest un-measured neighbour — the enum payload — is
// correct at compile AND at run. The program is UNCHANGED; only the reading is.
//
// Provenance: recorded 2026-08-18 in memory bug_zone_mut_reborrow_thin as one
// of three "still-open LOUD neighbors" of the D3 arc, never rowed; its evidence
// file sandbox/d3diag/p09*.logos no longer exists. Re-measured and rowed here.
// ⚠ PRICED 2026-09-08 (round 2026-09-08-fatrepr): THE ROW IS THREE ENGINES, NOT
// ONE SITE. A ceiling probe that gives `register_struct`'s ptr-to-struct field
// branch the fact it lacks (`ref_repr_of(field) == FatZoneMut` -> the 16B
// storage type, the arm four sibling branches already use) makes this program
// compile rc 0 and makes five constructed-and-RUN neighbours correct in both
// halves (`zone_of` read back through a named field, a tuple-struct field, a
// nested field, a write-through, and a `self: &mut` method receiver). But under
// `LOGOS_VERIFY_LAYOUT=1` it STILL aborts (5 disagreements -> 4), now naming the
// other two engines:
//     [product] H: size — mono_abi_layout says 8, llvm::DataLayout says 16
//     [product] H: size — sema_abi_layout says 8, llvm::DataLayout says 16
// `layout_of` is the only one of four engines that counts the field fat. Doors
// in SERIES: closing this row means carrying the same fact into
// `mono_abi_layout` and `sema_abi_layout` as well, with LOGOS_VERIFY_LAYOUT=1 as
// the acceptance oracle — the always-on cross-check alone would pass at one
// third of the work. Corpus radius: 3173 arrivals at the branch, none of them
// fat; no struct under tests/ or stdlib/ holds a `&mut` to a #[zone_mut] type.
package zonemut_fat_ref_struct_field_layout_abort;
#[zone_mut] struct Box2 { v: i64 }
struct H { r: &mut Box2 }
fn main() -> i32 {
    return 0i32;
}
